" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438074} {:answer/id #uuid "855857a7-7338-5129-b4f4-752ae0f7d9dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39b56f35-4411-58e8-91b8-70740004bb8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438074} :answer-field/id #uuid "345c1cd0-794d-566a-9e4b-9b18bedff524" :answer-field/key "$5v-1=5v-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439066}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6480ee2c-c900-5448-85b3-32f94538971e" :question/math-academy-id "q-288074" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9v-5 & =4v+2 \\\\ 9v-5-4v+5 & =4v+2-4v+5 \\\\ 5v & =7 \\\\ v & =\\frac{7}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $9v-5=4v+2$ has the unique solution $v=\\frac{7}{5}.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2v+3 & =2v+7 \\\\ 2v+3-2v & =2v+7-2v \\\\ 3 & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $v.$ Therefore, the equation $2v+3=2v+7$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5v-1 & =5v-1 \\\\ 5v-1-5v & =5v-1-5v \\\\ -1 & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $v.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $2v+3=2v+7$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff4e9141-5743-55f1-a8be-3e28cb047eca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id 